SM(392,{"n":"Deuteronomy 5 Part 2","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 5 Part 2.mp3","d":2432.2,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.88,"And you shall not make for yourself an image, neither any likeness of anything in heaven above, or in the earth beneath, or in the waters under the earth."],[30.24,"You shall not bow down to them or serve them, because I am the Lord your God, a jealous God, repaying the sins of the fathers upon the children to the third and fourth generation of those who hate me, but showing mercy to thousands who love me and keep my commandments."],[47.28,"Then there's the second piece or second commandment."],[50.26,"If you break it here."],[51.78,"Not to make any of these images."],[54.36,"Now, sometimes, sometimes some of our friends stop there."],[58.88,"They do not make any of these images."],[61.72,"Obvious problem with that, with just what we've read so far, is that we already got this commandment in Exodus 20."],[69.08,"Before we even got out of the book of Exodus, God was telling them to make graven images of things in heaven like cherubim, and of things on the earth like trees and fruit and things that crawl upon the ground, like the broad serpent in the book of Numbers."],[90.82,"So it's not just you can't draw a picture, okay, of anything."],[96.64,"Not what it's saying, because there's a rest of this, which is bowing down to them and serving them."],[103.56,"Now, again, bowing."],[107.72,"It's a shame I have to say this, but I do."],[110.81,"People with PhDs on YouTube seem to not understand this entirely."],[114.65,"When it says you will not bow down to them, that does not mean that, like bowing or making a what we call a matanya or that kind of thing in front of a picture is a sin."],[128.09,"Yes, Japanese people are, you know, Japanese call, I refuse to bow, I will not bow to greet."],[135.3,"Like, okay. Bowing down, the phrase translating bag down here has to do with worship."],[143.38,"Acts of worship."],[144.66,"And then serving."],[148.27,"Is again talking about doing what we call services."],[152.33,"Liturgic. Participating in liturgical services."],[155.99,"This is about worship."],[157.77,"This is saying don't worship idols."],[159.61,"It's very simple."],[161.21,"Okay. Idolatry is a particular thing."],[166.65,"Okay. Drawing a picture is not idolatry."],[170.33,"Ever. Ever. There is no picture that you can draw that is idolatry."],[175.85,"You can draw a picture that's blasphemous."],[177.77,"You can draw a picture that's right, obscene."],[180.65,"You can draw a picture that's."],[182.3,"But drawing a picture can never be idolatry, because that's what idolatry is."],[186.22,"Idolatry involves an act of worship, not an act of drawing or sculpting."],[187.9,"Okay And so the act of worship is what idolatry is."],[198.74,"And it's particularly acts of worship which use an idol, which use an image of the divine or of a spirit, in order to manipulate it, in order to get it to do what you want it to do ritually."],[214.36,"That's idolatry. Iconography is a whole other thing."],[221.96,"Not just, I'm not just talking about orthodox iconography, it's not idolatry."],[227.16,"Okay. Forget about that."],[229.24,"We're going back before there was a thing called the Orthodox Church."],[233.04,"Okay? When it was still called Israel."],[235.44,"We're gonna go back to the pagan world."],[237.84,"In the pagan world, there was idolatry, there were idols, and there was iconography."],[248.88,"If you went into a pagan temple, there was an idol there of the God that was used in worship for this purpose."],[260.7,"That they believed was indwelt by the spirit they were worshiping, that they offered food and sacrifices to."],[267.92,"That's idolatry. And then on the walls, there were frescoes."],[277.94,"Telling stories and myths."],[280.11,"Sometimes about that god, sometimes about one of the heroes that might be buried next to the temple."],[285.68,"That's iconography. It's pagan iconography."],[288.8,"Okay, it's not the same thing."],[293.28,"They're just not remotely the same thing, even in a pagan context."],[300.48,"Judaism is not supposed to practice idolatry."],[306.53,"Don't have idols, no idol in the temple."],[310.55,"No idol in the temple."],[312.23,"Jewish synagogues, no idols."],[314.95,"Guess what the temple and the synagogues were covered with?"],[318.79,"All over the walls, mosaic floors"],[320.03,"Iconography. They had all this iconography."],[327.45,"Not idolatry. It's a different thing."],[333.14,"And so Christianity comes along."],[336.66,"Also doesn't have idols."],[339.16,"We don't sacrifice anything to a statue."],[342.6,"We don't have a statue of Christ."],[346.06,"That we believe that Christ indwells, that we offer sacrifices to."],[349.9,"But we have iconography on the walls and things"],[350.26,"Don't do that."],[357.0,"This isn't ambiguous."],[358.92,"It's the fact that people can't like I it it beggars belief for me."],[365.45,"Like, again, any pagan could tell an ancient pagan who was an idolater could tell you the difference between an icon and an idol."],[376.73,"These are people who worshipped idols."],[379.15,"Knew the difference between the two."],[381.25,"Let alone people who don't worship idols."],[388.45,"This is pointing at the practice of idolatry."],[392.45,"Okay. The practice of idolatry."],[394.53,"Because it includes even idolatrous worship of the true God."],[399.77,"Like the golden calf in Exodus."],[404.79,"Where Aaron said, this is Yahweh pointing at the bull statue who brought you out of Egypt."],[413.61,"Doesn't matter that that he called he claimed that was an idol of the real God."],[417.13,"It's the idol worship that's the problem."],[421.09,"Yeah. And nobody accidentally worshipped the pomegranate trees on the walls in the temple."],[431.09,"That was just such a beautiful tree."],[432.45,"I felt like I had to offer a bowl to it."],[434.37,"Or the fresco of Nella or something."],[436.21,"Yes. Like no one walked into the synagogue and was like, what a beautiful depiction of the three holy youths in the furnace."],[443.89,"I think I will kill a goat and. sprinkle the blood right here"],[450.17,"The core of the problem, the core of the problem, the reason people don't see it, honestly, is that they're so disconnected from the concept of what worship actually is."],[461.29,"Like most of the people we're talking about who don't know the difference between an icon and an idol don't believe that they uh have have a religion in which there are no sacrifices."],[472.41,"We'll put it that way."],[475.55,"In the Christian religion, there's a sacrifice, the Eucharist."],[478.45,"But we're talking about people who have a religion that is certainly Christian themed and derived."],[487.22,"But which has no sacrifice in it."],[490.18,"it. And since they have no sacrifice from the perspective of an ancient person, I'll put this way"],[497.74,"So this is me trying to be nice and failing."],[501.58,"From the perspective of an ancient person, there's no worship going on."],[507.34,"If there's no sacrifice."],[516.92,"You're singing hymns together."],[519.24,"Very lovely. But an ancient person would not see any worship happening there if there's no sacrifice going on."],[528.09,"They would say, Oh, when do you worship your god?"],[530.85,"This is a very nice meeting."],[533.31,"Because it's just it's something it would be something else from an ancient person's perspective."],[537.93,"And so, since the difference between an idol and an icon is essentially worship, if you don't understand what worship is, you're not gonna understand the difference."],[546.01,"Just de facto."],[548.73,"It's all gonna kind of seem the same to you."],[551.53,"A picture's a picture, a statue's a statue, but"],[556.26,"Um, but yeah, that's the core."],[561.22,"Because none of them would assert that anyone was killing a goat over that picture of Noah's Ark on the synagogue wall."],[568.02,"They'd appreciate how absurd that is."],[571.12,"But that's what it would mean to worship that picture of Noah's Ark."],[577.64,"Well, I don't think do there really is a difference between an idol like three-dimensional and an icon."],[586.04,"Like just the fact that one's a flat surface Well but you could get into the whole issue of bas relief and you know things."],[595.08,"Yeah. It's still roughly two dimensional."],[598.2,"Yeah. There really is a very distinct idea like realism, you know, like like if if you're trying to worship a god."],[607.25,"Like an idol, like a carved statue is like there's a very distinct well there any idols that are two dimensional are idols always starbar."],[619.65,"So you could are you could so if someone took say someone took a photo of a departed ancestor and offered sacrifices in front of it."],[630.89,"Oh, that's a Hindu thing, yeah."],[632.57,"Yeah, that's what I'm saying."],[633.61,"Yeah. So there's some piece of religion where you do that kind of thing where you can have a two dimensional idol."],[638.57,"But see again, the difference is the w the worship, the sacrifices, the right."],[644.57,"That's that's the difference."],[646.73,"And so the real clarity we have to have, which was just abundantly clear to ancient people."],[654.33,"There was no confusion of this."],[657.82,"Is not as clear to us as modern people, because we sa the idea that worship is sacrifice is less clear to us."],[668.9,"At least in Anglo culture."],[672.42,"Right in the United States."],[674.74,"It's been very much divorced from that."],[677.3,"But so this commandment, people who originally received it knew exactly what this was telling them not to do."],[684.92,"And it had nothing to do with having a portrait painted."],[691.56,"Or having a having something painted on the wall of their house."],[695.53,"Now notice. So a lot of people."],[698.41,"There's another difference with modern people."],[701.53,"A lot of modern folks read this, say, God is a jealous God."],[705.05,"Ooh. And then. repaying the sins of the fathers upon the children to the third and fourth generation of those who hate me"],[714.85,"You're gonna pick on kids and grandkids and great grandkids for stuff that great grandpa did?"],[722.98,"Finish the sentence."],[728.34,"Finish the sentence."],[731.42,"But showing mercy to thousands, not to thousands of people, to thousands of generations."],[740.08,"Who love me and keep my commandments."],[742.56,"The point is."],[744.69,"It's it's making this structure."],[746.29,"So it starts out, the reason it says to the third and fourth generation is gotta saying this is very serious."],[750.05,"is very serious Idolatry this sin."],[750.77,"You're not gonna escape"],[755.25,"If you participate in this, you're not gonna sort of escape from it unscathed."],[759.26,"And it's and it's not just gonna affect you."],[761.82,"The sins you commit don't just affect you."],[765.76,"Because, again, sin has been redefined."],[770.4,"Sin has been redefined for us modern people as, oh, you broke a rule."],[775.04,"So now God's mad at you."],[776.4,"So they read this and they say, oh, God's gonna punish great grandkid for a thing that great grandpa did."],[786.3,"Because it's just this external legal thing of crime and punishment."],[792.95,"That's not what sin is and how sin works."],[795.99,"Okay, and and and we we know this."],[799.85,"We can think of plenty of sins off the top of our head that if you engage in it, it's gonna affect your family, and that means it's gonna affect your kids in negative ways."],[811.06,"Even though you're the one doing it."],[814.63,"And things that start cycles in families that go on for generations."],[822.2,"But so even as God points that out, in terms of the seriousness of the sin of idolatry, he also adds this promise."],[831.52,"Like, yes, that happens, that plays. out"],[836.05,"But to the person who loves him and keeps his commandments, thousand generations, God continues to bless."],[845.25,"Meaning, God is the way out of that."],[847.33,"God is the one who breaks that cycle."],[850.13,"But the reason they go to third and fourth is that most people don't live long enough to be a great, great grandparent."],[860.53,"So this is right, like within your frame of lifespan."],[865.89,"But think of how many times Israel's fallen into sin."],[872.45,"And why does God say He's going to show mercy on them?"],[877.53,"The sake of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob."],[883.13,"Going back a lot of generations now to get to them."],[888.06,"That's. This is part of here's our basic building block."],[896.38,"Who is the son of Abraham?"],[900.76,"Who is in this generation of Abraham?"],[902.92,"The one who loves him and kee. the name of the Lord your God in vain, for the Lord will not cleanse him who takes his name in vain"],[914.92,"That I think is actually a better translation."],[917.0,"So you gotta be fair."],[918.44,"That's because a lot of, I think the King James has God will not hold him guiltless."],[920.68,"Yeah, that's what I said"],[928.29,"And see, that lends itself, that reading lends itself to sort of that modern view of sin."],[933.35,"Whereas cleanse is more accurate to the original concept."],[939.0,"Um, and I know we talked about some of this is review from Exodus 20, the stuff that's the same, but taking the name of the Lord in vain does not refer to saying the word God or the name Jesus, or the name Jesus Christ, possibly with the middle initial you've made up."],[959.41,"As a curse word."],[961.25,"That's not good."],[962.29,"You shouldn't do that."],[963.17,"that. But's not primarily what this is talking about"],[967.14,"Uh, and so just walking around saying daggum it or gosh darn it, like, aw heck."],[975.98,"That's that's not you avoiding breaking this commandment."],[980.3,"Okay. Taking the name of the Lord does not just mean saying it out loud."],[986.06,"Okay. Taking the name of the Lord in vain, you take the name of the Lord, you receive the name of the Lord, when you are part of the nation which is called by his name."],[995.95,"So in this case, being an Israelite."],[997.95,"In our case, being called a Christian, calling yourself a Christian, includes whose name?"],[1004.67,"Christ. So the idea being when you identify yourself with God, then what does that mean?"],[1013.73,"That means everything you do reflects on God."],[1022.02,"Why is it such a disgrace when there's some scandal about some pastor or preacher or leader who gets caught doing something horrible?"],[1032.26,"People get caught doing that same stuff all the time."],[1035.3,"It's not, it doesn't even make the news."],[1038.18,"But somebody claims to be a man of God and they do it, and rightly, it's a huge scandal."],[1044.82,"That's the warning God is giving here"],[1045.06,"That's the warning God is giving here."],[1046.1,"ning God is giving here War."],[1049.54,"You're gonna call yourself a Christian"],[1056.64,"You're calling yourself an Israelite."],[1058.32,"You're gonna call yourself one of God's people."],[1060.97,"You're taking his name upon yourself."],[1063.61,"And so everything you do is reflect on him."],[1066.99,"People used to have a, I don't know if it's still true anymore, but people used to really have a sense of this with their family names."],[1075.49,"Somebody's son has their last name and they know it's their son, goes out and does something publicly."],[1081.75,"Bring shame on the whole family."],[1083.93,"Like that idea was, I think, more current in the past than it is now."],[1088.09,"Probably is still current in small towns where everybody kind of knows everybody."],[1092.86,"Or people who are really infamous, yeah."],[1095.5,"Um, for doing truly right, but that's what this is about."],[1101.02,"So this goes far beyond just that."],[1104.35,"Uh this is about everything we do publicly, everything we say public."],[1108.13,"If we're going to identify ourselves with God, then the way we conduct ourselves needs to reflect who God is."],[1118.39,"And when it doesn't, we are breaking this commandment."],[1123.19,"This is the issue, remember, that got Moses barred from entering the land of Canaan."],[1134.23,"God told him, go out, speak to the rock, I'll give them water from the rock"],[1134.51,"Remember? And what did Moses do?"],[1141.55,"He went and said, Must I bring you water from this rock?"],[1145.15,"And then struck it with his rod."],[1147.73,"And what did we say was the problem there?"],[1149.57,"He was misrepresenting God."],[1154.29,"That was his primary job to represent God to the people."],[1157.57,"He misrepresented God."],[1159.17,"He took the name of the Lord in vain."],[1162.78,"That's the sin here."],[1168.06,"Verse 12, observe the Sabbath day to keep it holy, as the Lord your God commanded you."],[1174.46,"Okay, now observe does not mean look at."],[1177.1,"Keep it holy, remember means set apart, meaning you treat it differently than other days"],[1187.3,"Six days you shall labor and do all your works, but the seventh day is the Sabbath, the Lord your God."],[1192.74,"In it you shall do no work, you, your son, or your daughter, your male servant, your female servant, your ox, your donkey, and all of your cattle, and your resident alien dwelling among you, that your male servant and your female servant may rest as well as you."],[1208.98,"Remember, you were a servant, really a slave, in the land of Egypt, and the Lord your God brought you out from there by a mighty hand and by an outstretched arm."],[1220.9,"Therefore, the Lord your God ordered you to guard the Sabbath day and to sanctify it."],[1223.3,"Um Okay, so what's going on there?"],[1236.06,"But it's a gift that requires their trust."],[1240.7,"So there was also a Sabbath year that they never followed."],[1244.6,"But most people, the vast majority of people at Israel who are receiving this commandment, are people who are doing subsistence farming."],[1253.4,"So a bad crop yield means they're losing one or more of their children to starvation."],[1258.92,"Quite literally. Subsistence farming, survival farming."],[1264.08,"And so telling them to take one day a week off where they don't go out and work the fields requires an immense amount of trust in God."],[1276.92,"Taking a year off required more than they had."],[1282.68,"That's why they never did it."],[1285.48,"But uh requires an immense amount of trust in God."],[1289.58,"To do what he said he was going to do to keep his promises."],[1292.86,"We've seen object lessons about this."],[1294.78,"Remember, the manna would fall for six days."],[1297.82,"If they tried to save any overnight, it would rot, except they would get twice as much on Friday."],[1305.95,"And then that would not rot."],[1308.27,"So they'd have food on the Sabbath and wouldn't have to go gather."],[1311.43,"Um again, what's that?"],[1314.23,"That's calling on you to trust and then God paying off that trust."],[1318.49,"By keeping his promise on this little thing."],[1320.67,"To show this."],[1322.03,"So why do we get this big long list?"],[1324.11,"Well, this big long list is cutting off all the ways you're gonna think of to get around this."],[1330.61,"You'd be like, well, I'm resting, but I'm gonna send my slaves out there to work the field."],[1337.49,"I'm gonna yes, I'm gonna have animals pulling the plow."],[1340.53,"I'm not pushing a plow."],[1343.33,"This ox is dragging the plow."],[1345.57,"I'm just standing here supervising."],[1347.95,"Uh hey, I hired this guy who's not an Israelite."],[1352.36,"He doesn't have to keep the Sabbath."],[1353.16,"He's gonna go out there and work for me on uh on the Sabbath"],[1359.34,"That's these are all the ways."],[1361.52,"And God is saying, nope, nope, nope, nope, nope, nope, nope, nope."],[1366.5,"Your job is not to find a way around this."],[1370.1,"Sorry, huge amount of industry in New York City today."],[1373.54,"Um. Your job is to follow this and trust in God."],[1378.04,"And that's why he points to."],[1381.73,"It's not just like, hey, remember, you guys used to be slaves."],[1385.89,"You gotta treat your slaves nice."],[1388.07,"Which is one way you can read this."],[1389.99,"Couple problems with that."],[1390.95,"Number one, the people he's talking to now, this time, weren't"],[1394.23,"t. But number two, the point is not, the emphasis is not on the fac that they were slaves"],[1401.64,"It's that God came and saved them with a mighty outstretched."],[1406.42,"That's the point he's making."],[1407.78,"He's like, I did that."],[1409.64,"You think I can't cover you for one day worth of work at the fields?"],[1413.64,"You think I'm gonna let you starve to death?"],[1417.08,"If you take a day off like I told you to?"],[1420.89,"That's what God is pointing to here."],[1424.67,"That's what God is pointing to here."],[1426.59,"And the overall system of this, is trying to show them what."],[1433.25,"Is that this isn't really your efforts?"],[1437.01,"This is a very modern and timely lesson, especially in America."],[1440.57,"Because we're all self-made men here."],[1442.89,"Everything I have, I earned my gum."],[1448.49,"We all started as nothing living in a log cabin."],[1452.03,"And worked our way up from nothing, and everything we have, we built and we achieved and we did it."],[1459.13,"And this is God pointing out to them."],[1461.45,"Uh-uh. No. If you have good crops, it's because God gave you good crops."],[1469.78,"You could go out there and work seven days a week as long as there's daylight and still get horrible crops."],[1477.7,"It's not in your control."],[1480.76,"And by the way, you didn't choose when and where and to whom you were gonna be born."],[1485.02,"Like you none of that."],[1486.88,"You don't choose whether you're gonna be healthy or sickly."],[1489.76,"None of that, none of that, none of that."],[1491.46,"What skills you're gonna have, what you're not gonna have, what intellectual capa capabilities you'll have and not have."],[1497.14,"None of that was up to you."],[1499.55,"All of that comes from God."],[1500.75,"And so this is a reminder."],[1504.21,"This is a reminder that what success you have is a blessing from God, not your own achievement for you to take pride in and flaunt over other people and accuse other people who don't have the blessings you've received of being lazy or stupid or evil or whatever else."],[1524.07,"That's what that's what uh God is getting at here."],[1529.03,"But so there's a whole system of these things."],[1530.95,"It's not just time-wise."],[1533.19,"It's not just you don't exploit every moment of your time in pursuit of whatever."],[1537.51,"So remember, you don't you don't harvest all the way to the edges of the field."],[1542.81,"You don't right, you don't go to the limits of everything."],[1545.85,"You don't try to extract every ounce of value, every, you know, every bit of"],[1551.62,"And so there's there's a a balanced element there."],[1558.54,"And again, if they're following tithing, they're not spending."],[1562.38,"They're not using a hundred percent of everything."],[1564.68,"10% of it's going."],[1566.3,"That's the idea."],[1567.99,"The idea is it is not our role as humans to try to exploit everything to the maximum, whether we're talking about time, whether we're talking about territory, whether we're talking about right, anything."],[1581.03,"It's not a resource for us to sort of fully exploit and then take credit for."],[1588.55,"And so part of now, some folks have this idea, that the Sabbath gets like transferred to Sunday."],[1601.53,"Sunday's now the Sabbath."],[1603.33,"Uh this is a peculiarity afflicting primarily English speakers, because we have pagan names for our days of the week, unlike most Christian people."],[1614.61,"But you just you can just look at Spanish, for example, where Saturday is called Sabado."],[1621.41,"Guess what that means?"],[1623.97,"The Sabbath. And what we call Sunday, they call Domingo."],[1631.06,"The Lord's Day."],[1632.76,"Kiraiki in Greek."],[1634.38,"All these other Christian calendars actually have Christian names for the days of the week."],[1638.06,"And what we call Saturday is still called the Sabbath."],[1642.87,"And what we call Sunday is called the Lord's Day."],[1645.03,"Sabbath and Lord's Day are two different things."],[1647.35,"And you come to understand that very quickly if you actually read any of the canons of the ecumenical councils."],[1653.55,"So for example, Council of Nicaea, verse 1."],[1658.35,"We don't consecrate the Eucharist during Lent, except on the Sabbath and the Lord's Day."],[1670.11,"So weekdays, what we call weekdays, you don't consecrate these."],[1675.31,"You don't fast, meaning fasting is loosened when every week."],[1681.15,"The Sabbath and the Lord's Day."],[1684.11,"They're still two separate things in Christian observance."],[1688.91,"But we're told, in for example, the Cynoxarian of Basca, that the apostles trans.ferred the dignity of the Sabbath to the Lord's day"],[1702.8,"Meaning that is the day that is set apart and holy, because that is the day that Christ rose from the dead."],[1711.6,"So the seventh day of the week, because the resurrection was a future hope, because rest in the kingdom was a future hope, the seventh day of the week was made holy to represent that."],[1731.22,"Now that it has become a reality in the resurrection of Christ, it's the first day of the week."],[1739.86,"So that is the idea."],[1741.14,"So it is still considered in the Orthodox Church to be a sin to do unnecessary work on the Sabbath."],[1748.1,"Or on feast days that are treated as Sabbaths, the same way the feast days of the Torah were treated as Sabbaths."],[1754.98,"Now, notice though, we have unnecessary work."],[1760.66,"So we try to avoid the kind of weird legalisms of pushing an elevator button is kindling a fire if it's electric."],[1769.3,"But if it's a pneumatic elevator, then it's fine."],[1773.38,"We'd sort of avoid all of that legalistic issue and just say, look, you don't do unnecessary work on the Sabbath."],[1782.58,"If you're a doctor and you're saving people's lives. go to it on the Lord's Day"],[1788.2,"That's necessary and good work."],[1791.8,"No spreadsheets need to be produced on the Lord's Day."],[1797.8,"Honor your father and mother in the manner the Lord your God commanded you, that it may be well with you, and you may be a long time in the land your the Lord your God is giving you."],[1807.4,"Say Paul will later point out that this is this commandment has a promise attached to it."],[1813.26,"That if you do this, you will live for a long time."],[1817.62,"In the land that the Lord is uh giving."],[1821.62,"And remember, we've talked about before."],[1823.42,"I'm gonna move a little more quickly through these other ones because we did really talk about you, and by the time anyone is listening to this. recording, or you sitting here now, you can go back and listen to the Exodus 20 recording where we went into more detail on each of these"],[1834.74,"Remember, honor your father and your mother does not mean do what they say."],[1837.94,"Sorry, parents. Umor your father and mother means you live your life in a way."],[1845.47,"We were just talking about this in terms of taking the name of the Lord in vain."],[1849.01,"You live your life in a way that it brings honor to your father and your mother."],[1853.97,"So that when people see how you live and who you are, they they assume, rightly or wrongly, that your parents were wonderful people who raised you right."],[1864.79,"As opposed to the opposite."],[1866.27,"Living your life in a way that brings shame."],[1869.17,"To your parents."],[1870.25,"And sometimes living your life in a way that brings honor to your parents might mean not doing what they tell you to, because they're sinners too."],[1879.11,"And what they want you to do may be for all kinds of reasons, other than it's the right thing to do."],[1885.2,"And so you do the right thing either way, and you are still bringing honor, to your father and mother."],[1894.26,"You shall not murder."],[1896.58,"Don't kill people."],[1898.58,"We had an extended discussion of that in Exodus 20."],[1901.78,"So I will refer you back to that."],[1904.98,"You shall not commit adultery."],[1906.74,"Again, we had an extended discussion of that."],[1909.3,"There's the very obvious, remember."],[1913.12,"You shall not steal."],[1914.0,"And these are all identical"],[1914.68,"We talked about that in detail."],[1916.92,"Exodus 20. I mean, the wording's identical in Deuteronomy 5 and Exodus 20."],[1922.36,"You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor."],[1926.76,"We talked about how that is not talking about lying."],[1929.96,"Sorry, Emmanuel Kant."],[1931.96,"Um that I mean, that is his best argument for a categorical imperative."],[1938.6,"Because his point is not just, well, if everybody see a lot of a lot of his arguments about categorical imperatives kind of devolve to, well, if everybody did it, that would be horrible, so you can't do it."],[1952.46,"Which is in general not a very good argument."],[1956.0,"Because you can propose all kinds of situations in which, yeah, everybody shouldn't do it all the time, but in this situation, you in particular maybe should."],[1965.57,"But this is why this is a better argument from Kant, because Kant's argument is for you to successfully lie, if you're in that situation where you need to lie, to protect someone's life, say."],[1978.77,"The only way that works, the only way your lie could be successful is if in general everyone tells the truth."],[1986.77,"Because if everyone lied all the time, no one would believe anyone."],[1992.85,"No one would trust everyone."],[1994.53,"And so that necessary lie in that particular situation wouldn't work if everyone lied all the time."],[2001.41,"And therefore, there has to be a general overarching rule against lying"],[2007.93,"So that's why I say it's a better argument."],[2010.09,"I'm not sold on deontology and ethics, but it is a better argument."],[2015.61,"I'm given credit where credit is due."],[2018.97,"But this isn't talking about lying."],[2021.21,"This isn't talking about do you lie to protect someone's life?"],[2023.93,"The answer is yes, you do."],[2026.19,"The answer is not, is it okay to not tell someone horrible true things that will hurt them deeply?"],[2032.83,"Of course, you should not tell someone horrible true things that would hurt them deeply."],[2037.41,"If you find someone unattractive, you don't have to tell them that."],[2041.05,"Especially not repeatedly."],[2043.62,"That's unless it's jewels, then I need to tell him repeatedly."],[2044.66,"That's right But you know, there are all kinds of things that are best left without saying, and that's not dishonest."],[2055.15,"Um this is specifically bearing false witnesses, very literally, you do not testify falsely, like in a hearing, in a dispute, you do not give false testimony that will harm someone else."],[2070.13,"You do not use your testimony, your word, giving your word to do harm to other people."],[2077.43,"That is what it is against."],[2079.83,"And again, we had a longer discussion of that."],[2083.51,"Under uh Exodus 20."],[2086.63,"And then finally. we will end here at the end of the Ten Commandments, even though we're not at the end of the chapter"],[2092.83,"You shall not covet your neighbor's wife, and you shall not covet your neighbor's house, neither his field, his male servant, his female servant, his ox, his donkey, or his cattle, or anything belonging to your neighbor."],[2105.87,"We talked about the division issue, already, so we don't have to cover that again."],[2110.53,"But why is this commandment important?"],[2113.74,"Because we commented, we were talking about the division issue."],[2115.98,"Like coveting your neighbor's wife is kind of already covered under adultery."],[2120.3,"You'd think. But is it?"],[2123.82,"If it's just in your brain, have you committed adultery yet?"],[2128.3,"Well, this commandment says yes."],[2130.94,"That's the importance of this commandment."],[2131.9,"You covet his donkey, you haven't actually stolen it"],[2138.42,"Still a sin."],[2139.96,"And so there's this, again, today we would call it a meme, that Christ sort of makes the law of Moses more strict."],[2150.44,"When he says, like hating your brother in your heart is the same as killing him, or looking at a woman with lust in your heart as committing adultery with her."],[2158.74,"It's like, no, that's the coveting."],[2161.46,"That's the commandment about coveting."],[2163.8,"That's what this commandment is about."],[2166.54,"It's not just about desiring things that other people have."],[2170.07,"It includes that."],[2171.51,"But it's about all of the thoughts."],[2176.08,"That precede all the commandments we just talked about."],[2184.37,"So it does just out of the blue commit adultery."],[2187.33,"There's a whole series of thoughts that lead to other actions that precede that action."],[2194.98,"You don't just steal something, there's a whole series of thoughts."],[2199.72,"You don't just randomly murder someone."],[2202.29,"There's a whole series of thoughts."],[2204.71,"And resentments and hatreds that precede that that lead up to it."],[2209.19,"Those are sinful too."],[2211.51,"Why is it important that we say those are sinful too?"],[2214.79,"It's important we say those are sinful too, because that's the place where we need to head it off and stop it."],[2224.08,"Because what's the alternative?"],[2225.52,"The alternative is we say to people, oh no, you can have all those thoughts."],[2229.52,"That's all fine."],[2230.48,"It's all fine until you do something."],[2234.32,"How much more evil is gonna get done if you send people that message?"],[2239.28,"Oh no, feel free to just dwell on that in your mind."],[2241.92,"That's that's cool."],[2243.81,"Like that's why."],[2247.06,"No, it's already sinned at that point because that's where we need to stop it."],[2250.1,"That's where you need to repent."],[2251.78,"You don't let it get all the way to because the further it goes, the more consequences there are."],[2258.26,"there. And the more damage is to you and the people around you, the further it goes"],[2259.42,"Yeah. And so the further back we can catch it."],[2268.95,"Before that damage is done."],[2271.24,"Because we've talked about this before with repentance."],[2274.04,"Repentance is not just, oh, I feel bad."],[2276.7,"It's working to repair the damage you've done."],[2280.08,"But even as you do that, there's a lot of bells you can't unring."],[2284.4,"Yes. Yeah, you kill it."],[2286.96,"You can't bring the person back to life."],[2288.58,"Once you've said something out loud to someone, you can't really unsay it."],[2293.46,"You could apologize, you could do everything you can to make it up to that person, but you can't reverse time and not say it."],[2300.74,"it. It's still out there, still happened"],[2304.67,"The damage was still done."],[2306.49,"It's like you break a leg."],[2310.39,"It can heal up, but will I betcha for the rest of your life now and then your body's gonna remind you about that time you broke that leg."],[2319.61,"Like it's still a thing that happened."],[2322.11,"And so this commandment, again, is for us."],[2327.99,"Catching it as far back as possible."],[2331.19,"The first inklings."],[2333.21,"Of thinking and moving in the wrong direction."],[2335.41,"That's where we catch it."],[2336.61,"That's where we repent."],[2339.11,"Because it's much easier to heal that than everything that's going to happen as it as it progresses."],[2342.07,"that. And notice I said commandments again"],[2349.47,"All of the commandments are gifts."],[2352.19,"And this is something we owe culturally to Martin Luther."],[2356.93,"This whole emphasis on what he called the first use of the law."],[2360.05,"These commandments are just here to condemn us."],[2363.73,"Just here to point out how sinful and horrible we are."],[2366.53,"No, these are gifts to us."],[2370.29,"To help us know how to live."],[2373.38,"To help us catch ourselves, check ourselves."],[2376.71,"Avoid doing these horrible things and suffering these damaging consequences."],[2381.69,"God revealing these commandments to us is a blessing and a gift to us."],[2385.81,"And that's why later on Deuteronomy it's gonna say the one who does these things will find life in them, which St."],[2393.33,"Paul quotes in Romans, agreeing with it."],[2396.93,"Sorry, Martin Luther."],[2399.25,"I'll end there."],[2401.57,"So thank you, everybody."],[2403.89,"We will pick up here in the middle of chapter five next time."],[2409.65,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2417.01,"Father Stephen's email address is whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2422.37,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":22.88,"lv":2,"h":"5:8-10 - No graven image","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reads <b>5:8-10</b>: no image or likeness of anything in <b>heaven, earth, waters under the earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't <b>bow down</b> or <b>serve</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I am the Lord your God, a <b>jealous God</b>\" - sins of fathers to <b>3rd and 4th generation</b>; <b>mercy to thousands</b> who love me</li><li class=\"d0\">Second commandment (Orthodox/Protestant count)</li><li class=\"d0\">Some friends <b>stop at \"don't make images\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Problem: <b>Exodus 20</b> had same commandment - yet God told them to make images</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>cherubim</b> (heaven), <b>trees and fruit</b> (earth), <b>bronze serpent</b> in Numbers (crawling things)</li><li class=\"d0\">So not \"can't draw a picture of anything\" - <b>rest of the verse</b> matters: <b>bowing and serving</b></li></ul>"},{"t":135.3,"lv":2,"h":"Idolatry is about worship","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"People with PhDs on YouTube\" misread \"bow down\"</li><li class=\"d1\">bowing or a <b>metanoia</b> before a picture is <b>not</b> the sin - \"Japanese… I refuse to bow\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Bow down\" = <b>worship</b>; \"serve\" = <b>liturgical services</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Drawing a picture is not idolatry. <b>Ever.</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">can be <b>blasphemous, obscene</b> - never idolatry</li><li class=\"d1\">idolatry = <b>act of worship</b>, not drawing or sculpting</li><li class=\"d0\">Particularly worship using <b>an image of the divine or a spirit</b> to <b>manipulate it</b> ritually</li></ul>"},{"t":214.36,"lv":3,"h":"Idol vs iconography","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Iconography</b> a whole other thing - not just Orthodox iconography</li><li class=\"d0\">Go back <b>before the Orthodox Church</b> - to <b>Israel</b>, to the <b>pagan world</b></li><li class=\"d1\">pagan temple: <b>idol</b> of the god, believed <b>indwelt</b> by the spirit; <b>food and sacrifices</b> offered = idolatry</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>frescoes</b> on walls: stories, myths - of the god or <b>heroes buried next to the temple</b> = pagan iconography</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not remotely the same thing, even in a pagan context\"</li></ul>"},{"t":300.48,"lv":3,"h":"Judaism and Christianity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Judaism: <b>no idols</b> in temple or synagogue</li><li class=\"d1\">but walls, <b>mosaic floors</b> covered in <b>iconography</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christianity also no idols</li><li class=\"d1\">no <b>sacrifice to a statue</b>, no statue of Christ that Christ indwells</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>iconography</b> on the walls</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not ambiguous\" - any ancient <b>idolater</b> could tell icon from idol</li><li class=\"d0\">Points at <b>practice of idolatry</b> - includes idolatrous worship of the <b>true God</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>golden calf</b>: Aaron - \"this is <b>Yahweh</b> who brought you out of Egypt\" - still the problem</li><li class=\"d0\">Nobody worshiped the <b>pomegranate trees</b> in the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">nobody saw <b>three holy youths in the furnace</b> and thought \"I'll <b>kill a goat</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":450.17,"lv":2,"h":"Why people can't see the difference","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Core: disconnected from <b>what worship is</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Religion \"Christian themed\" but <b>no sacrifice</b> - Christianity has the <b>Eucharist</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ancient person: <b>no sacrifice = no worship</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"very lovely\" hymn singing - \"when do you worship your god?\" - just \"a very nice meeting\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Idol vs icon = <b>worship</b> → don't understand worship, <b>\"a picture's a picture, a statue's a statue\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">None would claim anyone <b>killing a goat</b> over <b>Noah's Ark</b> on the synagogue wall - that would be worship</li></ul>"},{"t":577.64,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: two-dimensional idols?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: isn't there a real difference between <b>3D idol and 2D icon</b>? bas relief - \"roughly two dimensional\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: photo of a <b>departed ancestor</b> with <b>sacrifices</b> before it? - <b>Hindu</b> practice → a <b>2D idol</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Answer: again the difference is <b>worship, sacrifices</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Clear to ancients, less so for us - <b>worship = sacrifice</b> divorced in <b>Anglo / US culture</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Original hearers knew exactly what it forbade - <b>nothing to do with a portrait</b> or wall painting</li></ul>"},{"t":695.53,"lv":2,"h":"Jealous God and the generations","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moderns hear \"<b>jealous</b>… sins of the fathers to the third and fourth generation\" → \"picking on grandkids?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Finish the sentence</b>\" - mercy to <b>thousands of generations</b>, not thousands of people</li><li class=\"d0\">Structure: \"3rd and 4th\" = idolatry is <b>very serious</b>, no escaping unscathed</li><li class=\"d0\">Sins <b>don't just affect you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moderns redefined sin: \"you broke a rule, God's mad\" - <b>external legal crime and punishment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not how sin works</li><li class=\"d0\">Sins that harm <b>family, kids</b>; <b>cycles</b> across generations</li><li class=\"d0\">Alongside the warning: <b>thousand generations</b> of blessing for those who love him</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God is the way out</b>, breaks the cycle</li><li class=\"d0\">3rd/4th = most don't live to <b>great-great-grandparent</b> - within <b>lifespan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Israel falls constantly - mercy <b>for the sake of Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b> - many generations back</li><li class=\"d1\">\"basic building block\" - who is <b>son of Abraham</b>?</li></ul>"},{"t":902.92,"lv":2,"h":"5:11 - The name in vain","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"will not <b>cleanse</b> him who takes his name in vain\"</li><li class=\"d1\">better than KJV \"hold him guiltless\" - <b>cleanse</b> fits the original, not the <b>modern view of sin</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not primarily <b>cursing</b> with \"God\" or \"Jesus Christ\" (+ \"made-up middle initial\") - shouldn't, but not the point</li><li class=\"d1\">\"daggum it\", \"gosh darn it\" - <b>not avoiding</b> the commandment</li></ul>"},{"t":980.3,"lv":3,"h":"Bearing the name","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">You <b>take/receive the name</b> when part of the nation <b>called by his name</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israelite; <b>Christian</b> - <b>Christ's</b> name</li><li class=\"d0\">Identify with God → <b>everything you do reflects on God</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>scandal</b> of a pastor or preacher caught - others do it and it's not news</li><li class=\"d0\">Like <b>family names</b>: son shames the whole family - still true in <b>small towns</b></li><li class=\"d0\">About everything we do and say <b>publicly</b> - when it doesn't reflect who God is, we break this</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses</b> barred from Canaan</li><li class=\"d1\">told to <b>speak to the rock</b>; said \"<b>must I bring you water</b>\" and <b>struck it</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>misrepresenting God</b> - \"took the name of the Lord in vain\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1168.06,"lv":2,"h":"5:12-15 - Sabbath","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reads <b>5:12-15</b>: observe the Sabbath to <b>keep it holy</b>; six days labor</li><li class=\"d1\">no work for you, children, servants, <b>ox, donkey, cattle, resident alien</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"remember you were a <b>slave</b> in Egypt… <b>mighty hand and outstretched arm</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Observe\" ≠ look at; \"keep it holy\" = <b>set apart</b>, treat differently</li><li class=\"d0\">A <b>gift that requires trust</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also a <b>Sabbath year</b> - never followed</li><li class=\"d0\">Most Israelites = <b>subsistence farmers</b> - bad yield = <b>losing children to starvation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a day off needs <b>immense trust</b>; a year off \"more than they had\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Manna</b>: rots overnight except <b>double on Friday</b> - trust then payoff</li></ul>"},{"t":1322.03,"lv":3,"h":"The long list closes loopholes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">List cuts off ways to get around it</li><li class=\"d1\">send <b>slaves</b> to work the field</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ox pulls the plow</b> - \"I'm just supervising\"</li><li class=\"d1\">hire a <b>non-Israelite</b> who needn't keep Sabbath</li><li class=\"d1\">God: \"<b>nope, nope, nope</b>\" - \"huge industry in New York City today\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Your job: <b>follow and trust</b>, not find a way around</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just \"you were slaves, treat slaves nice\" - one reading</li><li class=\"d1\">problems: these hearers <b>weren't</b> slaves; emphasis isn't on slavery</li><li class=\"d0\">Point: <b>God saved them</b> with a mighty arm</li><li class=\"d1\">\"You think I can't cover <b>a day's work</b>? You think I'll let you <b>starve</b>?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1437.01,"lv":3,"h":"Success is God's gift","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Timely lesson for <b>America</b>: \"self-made men\", \"log cabin\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God: good crops are <b>from God</b>; work seven days and still get horrible crops</li><li class=\"d0\">You didn't choose <b>when, where, to whom</b> born; <b>health</b>; <b>skills</b>; <b>intellect</b> - all from God</li><li class=\"d0\">Success = <b>blessing</b>, not achievement to <b>take pride in</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not to accuse the less blessed of being <b>lazy, stupid, evil</b></li><li class=\"d0\">A system, not just time</li><li class=\"d1\">don't <b>harvest to the edges</b> of the field</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tithing</b> - not 100% of everything, <b>10% goes</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not our role to <b>exploit everything to the maximum</b> - time, territory, anything</li><li class=\"d1\">not a resource to exploit then <b>take credit</b> for</li></ul>"},{"t":1588.55,"lv":2,"h":"Sabbath and the Lord's Day","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Idea that Sabbath <b>transferred to Sunday</b> - peculiar to <b>English speakers</b>, <b>pagan day names</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Spanish <b>Sabado</b> = Sabbath; <b>Domingo</b> = Lord's Day</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek <b>Kyriaki</b>; Saturday still \"Sabbath\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two different things</b> - see <b>canons of the ecumenical councils</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Nicaea 1</b> (as he cites): no consecrating the Eucharist in <b>Lent</b> except <b>Sabbath and Lord's Day</b>; fasting loosened both</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Synaxarion of Pascha</b>: apostles <b>transferred the dignity of the Sabbath</b> to the Lord's Day</li><li class=\"d1\">7th day = future hope of <b>rest in the kingdom</b>; now reality in the <b>resurrection</b> → <b>first day</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still a <b>sin</b> to do <b>unnecessary work</b> on Sabbath or Sabbath-like <b>feast days</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Avoid legalisms: <b>elevator button = kindling a fire</b> if electric, fine if pneumatic</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Doctor saving lives</b> on the Lord's Day - necessary and good</li><li class=\"d0\">\"No <b>spreadsheets</b> on the Lord's Day\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1797.8,"lv":2,"h":"5:16 - Honor father and mother","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Reads <b>5:16</b> - promise attached (<b>Paul</b> notes): <b>long life in the land</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moving faster - details in <b>Exodus 20</b> recording</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"<b>do what they say</b>\" - sorry, parents</li><li class=\"d1\">live so it <b>brings honor</b> to them; people assume wonderful parents</li><li class=\"d1\">sometimes means <b>not doing what they say</b> - \"they're sinners too\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1894.26,"lv":2,"h":"5:17-20 - Murder to false witness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>No murder</b>, <b>no adultery</b>, <b>no stealing</b> - extended discussion in <b>Exodus 20</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Wording <b>identical</b> in Deut 5 and Exodus 20</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Bear false witness</b> - not about lying generally</li><li class=\"d1\">\"sorry, <b>Emmanuel Kant</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1931.96,"lv":3,"h":"Kant's categorical imperative","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Best argument: a <b>necessary lie</b> (to protect a life) only works if <b>in general everyone tells the truth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ overarching rule against lying</li><li class=\"d1\">better than \"if everyone did it, horrible\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not sold on <b>deontology</b>\" - credit where due</li><li class=\"d0\">Not about lying: <b>yes you lie to protect a life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't have to tell <b>horrible true things</b> - \"unattractive\" - not dishonest</li><li class=\"d0\">Specifically <b>testifying falsely</b> - hearing, dispute - using your word to <b>harm others</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2086.63,"lv":2,"h":"5:21 - Do not covet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">End of Ten Commandments (not end of chapter)</li><li class=\"d0\">Reads <b>5:21</b>: neighbor's <b>wife</b>, house, field, servants, <b>ox, donkey, cattle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Division issue already covered</li><li class=\"d0\">Why important: wife coveting \"covered under adultery\"? - <b>in your brain</b> = committed? → <b>yes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">covet his donkey - haven't stolen it - <b>still sin</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Meme: Christ <b>makes Moses' law stricter</b> - hating = killing, lust = adultery</li><li class=\"d1\">no: that's the <b>coveting commandment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just desiring others' things - <b>all the thoughts that precede</b> the other commandments</li></ul>"},{"t":2211.51,"lv":3,"h":"Heading it off early","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Adultery, stealing, murder - preceded by <b>thoughts, resentments, hatreds</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why say those are sinful? <b>Where we stop it, repent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">alternative: \"all fine until you do something\" → <b>more evil done</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Further it goes = more <b>consequences, damage</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Repentance</b> = not \"I feel bad\" - <b>repairing the damage</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>can't unring bells</b>: can't revive the dead, can't unsay words</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>broken leg</b> - heals, still reminds you</li><li class=\"d0\">Catch <b>first inklings</b> of moving the wrong direction - easier to heal</li></ul>"},{"t":2342.07,"lv":2,"h":"Commandments are gifts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"All of the commandments are <b>gifts</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">owed culturally to <b>Martin Luther</b> - <b>first use of the law</b>: here to <b>condemn us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no: help us <b>know how to live</b>, <b>check ourselves</b>, avoid damaging consequences</li><li class=\"d0\">Later in Deuteronomy: \"the one who does these things will <b>find life in them</b>\" - <b>Paul</b> quotes in <b>Romans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Sorry, Martin Luther\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: <b>middle of Deuteronomy 5</b>"});
